    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "6",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Manoeuvring and Seakeeping",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Ship theory has traditionally been separated into two main areas",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "table",
        "table_caption": [],
        "table_body": "<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Manoeuvring\nThe aim is to study steering characteristics of vessels with forward speed and the response to the command of propulsion systems and control surfaces. This is done in calm water.</th>\n    <th>Sea-keeping\nThe aim is to study the behavior of the vessel in waves while keeping a constant speed and course.</th>\n  </tr>\n</table>",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Although both areas are concerned with the study of *motion*, *stability* and *control*, the separation allows one making assumptions that simplify the study in each case.",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "7",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Manoeuvring Models",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Nonlinear parametric models (classical and Lagrangian):"
        ],
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Obtained by fitting data from scaled model experiments.",
            "- Calm water models.",
            "- Horizontal motion models (surge-sway-yaw).",
            "- Not commonly available.",
            "- Restricted to a few speeds/loading conditions of the experiment."
        ],
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/1f3d48bc41896fbfe654affbd377c431aa6343eae1d22889ec0ba5e636a26492.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/8f19b17499289a9c24d513a2fdfc61bb550a0b4599a2ad3b8cb3671008227cdb.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "8",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Seakeeping Models",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/4003be491fbc8e6b6eb38bbe59bf682c6599d10c14568bb274de8d6fe3258e35.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Linear non-parametric models",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Obtained from hydrodynamic calculations based on simplifying assumptions:",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Constant course and speed.",
            "- Linear wave loads.",
            "- Potential theory.",
            "- Viscous effects can be added."
        ],
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "For the design of control systems, seakeeping models are very useful.",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "They provide preliminary models based on little data of the ship.",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "9",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Recent Results on a Unified Manoeuvring and Seakeeping Model",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- <strong>Fossen, T. I. and Ø. N. Smogeli.</strong> Nonlinear Time-Domain Strip Theory Formulation for Low-Speed Manoeuvring and Station-Keeping, <em>Modelling, Identification and Control,</em> <strong>MIC-25</strong>(4):201:221, 2004.",
            "- <strong>Fossen, T. I.</strong> A Nonlinear Unified State-Space Model for Ship Manoeuvring and Control in a Seaway, <em>Journal of Bifurcation and Chaos</em>, September 2005. (Plenary Talk ENOC'05, Eindhoven, The Netherlands).",
            "- **Perez, T. and T. I. Fossen.**  Kinematic Models for Sea-keeping and Manoeuvring of Marine Vessels. Modelling, Identification and Control, **MIC-28**(1):1-12, 2007.",
            "- <strong>Perez, T. and T. I. Fossen.</strong> Time-Domain Models of Marine Surface Vessels for Simulation and Control Design Based on Sea-keeping Computations (Plenary Talk). <em>Proc. of the IFAC MCMC'06, Lisbon, Portugal, September 20-22, 2006.</em>",
            "- **Ross, A., T. Perez and T. I. Fossen .** A Novel Manoeuvring Model Based on Low-Aspect Ratio Lift Theory and Lagrangian Mechanics. Proc. of the IFAC CAMS'07, Croatia."
        ],
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "10",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Unified Manoeuvring and Seakeeping Model for Time-Domain Simulation",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<strong>The</strong> <em><strong>Force-Transfer-Functions</strong></em> <strong>are computed using hydrodynamic SW (WAMIT, VERES or SEAWAY )</strong>",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/f20ee8f59ee386dd66951c4830e8be655e924ff52f07c05506e36c24f94e0e43.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/a9eacf6ae97b3ee384cea112d6fab52ec7b8801d63db5616e5ebf4cf8caaef54.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "*For 6 DOF this model will typically be represented by* *6 + 6 + 90 = 102 ODEs*",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "*which are computed using*",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "***hydrodynamic SW (WAMIT, VERES or SEAWAY )***",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "*These terms are found using experimental results/curve fitting or semi-empirical methods*",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "11",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Speed–Environment Envelope",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Hull supported by mostly by hydrostatic pressure (forces)",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/4756ac32911bb1bc07082a0526c51eed3d56b2a4ef7db471a82a989dbd2c39f5.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/e621c7609da9b52fbfadd7a64e9c7c0d9284d563e6849d1e5452c9f125701e25.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/6ace22c5dc2d9d0441bbe154d32ee2af26100ad6cbee4b96e1859f53227b7f58.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/745c78c6f1c10005c8bafafb8a7af9ab4cb43c8b2ae82304d3842e743b7a82d2.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Hydrostatic and hydrodynamic forces; Lift",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/6a5ab88da1f8f2ad36abc706ae7eab14e716565a807d367bee24c3e550f8e692.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Aero and hydrodynamic forces; strong flow separation",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "12",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The 3 Speed Regimes for Control",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**Dynamic positioning systems**",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- 3D potential theory",
            "- 2D potential theory (strip theory)"
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**Manoeuvring/motion damping**",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- 2D potential theory (strip theory) up to *Froude numbers* of 0-3-0.4",
            "- 2.5 D potential theory for high-speed craft"
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/e621c7609da9b52fbfadd7a64e9c7c0d9284d563e6849d1e5452c9f125701e25.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/1ad3eb9d37c4f77ffc1aa8eebc6193f965fe3ac62aae440a7275d519fd442254.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/2be45ccc87066e09559e9f0209a5d88d1814bdd5b1104a45eae6b3210b147ac7.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Manoeuvring at moderate speed",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(transit)",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Manoeuvring at high speed",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(high-speed craft)",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Low-speed",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "maneuvering",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Station-keeping",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "0",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "1.5 m/s (3 knots)",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "….",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "…..",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "*Speed*",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "13",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Motion in Waves",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Motions and loads of floating structures due to waves can be separated into",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Wave-frequency: linearly excitations and motion in the wave frequency range. Periods in the range 5-20s",
            "- Higher than wave frequency (ringing & springing): nonlinear effects, which can produce resonance in TLPs, with natural periods of 2-4s."
        ],
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Slow and mean drift: nonlinear effects with mean value and sub harmonic excitation that can produce oscillations with natural periods of 20-30s."
        ],
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "14",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Motion and Control",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Then, motion control problems can have different objectives:",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- ***Control only the non-oscillatory  motion (wave filtering needed)***",
            "    - Autopilots,",
            "    - Dynamic positioning (DP)",
            "    - Thruster assisted position mooring (TAPMOOR)",
            "- ***Control only the oscillatory motion***",
            "    - Ride control of high speed vessels (roll and pitch stabilisation)",
            "    - Heave compensation of offshore structures",
            "- ***Control both***",
            "    - Dynamic positioning in extreme seas (DP + roll & pitch stabilisation)",
            "    - Autopilots with rudder roll stabilisation",
            "    - Unmanned Surface Vehicles USV"
        ],
        "page_idx": 14
    },
